# striim-testing-framework-utility settings.
#
# Copy this file to .env in the clone root (`cp .env.example .env`) and fill it in.
# Lines are KEY=value. Quotes, an `export ` prefix and trailing ` # comments` are allowed.
# A variable already set in your shell wins over the same key here.
# A relative path here is resolved against this file's directory.
# `striim-test doctor` checks this file and names anything wrong in it.
# Every setting, where it can be set and its default: docs/SETTINGS.md.

# --- Striim target --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your own Striim server: its root URL (no path), and a user allowed to create and drop apps. Leave
# STRIIM_URL unset to run in Docker mode instead: the first run downloads the Striim packages,
# builds a Striim image and starts a cluster (docs/RUN-YOUR-FIRST-TEST.md, "Docker mode").
# STRIIM_URL=http://striim.example.com:9080
# STRIIM_USER=admin
# STRIIM_PASS=
# Timeout on Striim REST calls, seconds: "600" (read), "10,600" (connect,read), or "0" for none.
# Login and read-only polls use (10,120); jar LOAD and UNLOAD use none.
# STRIIM_API_TIMEOUT=10,600
# The host Striim reaches every service by, when that differs from this machine's (default
# localhost; host.docker.internal for the Docker cluster).
# SLT_STRIIM_VIEW_HOST=
# Docker mode's license (COMPANY_NAME, CLUSTER_NAME, PRODUCT_KEY, LICENCE_KEY) is never read from
# this file: by default it comes from $STRIIM_HOME/conf/startUp.properties; otherwise export it in
# your shell or put it in the machine file (docs/SETTINGS.md).

# --- Infrastructure ownership ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every live run must say whether it owns the Striim cluster and the service containers it uses; a
# run with SLT_INFRA_OWNERSHIP unset is refused before it starts anything.
# shared (the default here): reuse whatever is already running, start what is missing, and never
# tear any of it down. SLT_KEEP_SERVICES=1 is required with it. Safe on a cluster that other people
# use.
# exclusive (opt-in): the run takes a fresh stack of its own, refuses to start if a Striim already
# answers on the endpoint, and tears everything down at the end (remove SLT_KEEP_SERVICES=1 for
# that). Set it only on a machine where nothing else uses that endpoint.
SLT_INFRA_OWNERSHIP=shared
SLT_KEEP_SERVICES=1

# --- Locations ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the live cases are. `striim-test run PATH` only runs cases under this folder, so it must
# cover the samples (samples/live and samples/code). Several roots: separate them with : (; on
# Windows).
SLT_LIVE_CASES=samples
# The project: case ids, example: and jar: paths are relative to it, and its .env is the one read.
# Only the shell's value says where that .env is.
# SLT_PROJECT_ROOT=
# The framework checkout.
# SLT_FRAMEWORK_HOME=
# The integration case root.
# SLT_INT_CASES=
# Live service definitions.
# SLT_SERVICES_DIR=scripts/live/services
# Integration service definitions.
# SLT_INT_SERVICES_DIR=scripts/integration/services
# Run directories and coordination files.
# SLT_STATE_DIR=scripts/live

# --- Running --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 0: turn off every service's pre_up hook.
# SLT_PRE_UP=
# Run a second, independent stack on the same machine: its containers and cleanup carry this
# prefix.
# SLT_STACK_PREFIX=

# --- The Docker Striim cluster --------------------------------------------------------------------
# CPUs the primary node may use; 0 is no limit. The license caps the CPUs a cluster counts (24 in
# the tested licenses), and each node counts every CPU it sees, so on a machine with more than 12
# CPUs cap both nodes, for example 12 each.
# SLT_STRIIM_PRIMARY_CPUS=0
# CPUs the second node may use; 0 is no limit.
# SLT_STRIIM_NODE_CPUS=0
# Java heap of each node. Lower it on a modest machine or before running several stacks.
# SLT_STRIIM_MEM_MAX=16384m
# Memory limit of each node's container; 0 is no limit.
# SLT_STRIIM_MEM_LIMIT=0
# Extra Java system properties for the nodes, for example -Djava.awt.headless=true.
# SLT_STRIIM_JAVA_SYSTEM_PROPERTIES=
# 1: fetch Teradata's JDBC driver from Maven Central and build it into the Striim image, for the
# teradata service. Teradata's licence for the driver applies (SERVICES.md, Teradata).
# SLT_TERADATA_JDBC=
# Host port of the console and REST API.
# SLT_STRIIM_HTTP_HOST_PORT=9080
# Host port of HTTPS.
# SLT_STRIIM_HTTPS_HOST_PORT=9081
# Host port of the primary's JMX Prometheus exporter.
# SLT_STRIIM_JMX_HOST_PORT=7071
# Host port of the second node's JMX exporter.
# SLT_STRIIM_NODE_JMX_HOST_PORT=7075
# Host port of the agent's JMX exporter.
# SLT_STRIIM_AGENT_JMX_HOST_PORT=7076
# Host port of the primary's JDWP remote debugger.
# SLT_STRIIM_DEBUG_HOST_PORT=8787
# For example, on a machine with more than 12 CPUs (set both here, or in your shell):
#   export SLT_STRIIM_PRIMARY_CPUS=12 SLT_STRIIM_NODE_CPUS=12
# Already have the Striim installers? Skip the first run's 6.3 GB download by exporting a manifest
# of them in your shell (not read from this file; docs/RUN-YOUR-FIRST-TEST.md has the format):
# export SLT_STRIIM_DEPS_MANIFEST=/path/to/deps-manifest.json

# --- Services -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A case lists the databases it needs under `requires:` in its test.yaml. Each one is started in
# Docker by the run, with test-only credentials, and nothing needs to be set here for that. To use
# your own instance instead, set its host (the first line of its block); the other settings default
# to the container's values, shown here. Credentials are left blank: unset, the container's apply.
# docs/SERVICES.md has every account, port and URL; docs/SETTINGS.md what each setting does.

# GCS emulator (gcs)
# SLT_GCS_HOST=localhost
# SLT_GCS_PORT=4443
# SLT_GCS_PROJECT=test-project
# SLT_GCS_SRC_BUCKET=slt-src
# SLT_GCS_TGT_BUCKET=slt-tgt
# SLT_GCS_HOST_PORT=4443
# SLT_GCS_TOKEN_HOST_PORT=4444
# SLT_GCS_CPUS=0.5
# SLT_GCS_EXTERNAL_URL=
# SLT_GCS_MEM_LIMIT=512m
# SLT_GCS_PUBLIC_HOST=
# SLT_TOKEN_CPUS=0.5
# SLT_TOKEN_MEM_LIMIT=512m
# SLT_GCS_VIEW_HOST=

# Kafka (kafka)
# SLT_KAFKA_HOST=localhost
# SLT_KAFKA_PORT=9092
# SLT_KAFKA_BROKER_PORT=19092
# SLT_KAFKA_REGISTRY_PORT=8081
# SLT_ZOOKEEPER_PORT=2181
# SLT_KAFKA_SRC_TOPIC=slt_src
# SLT_KAFKA_TGT_TOPIC=slt_tgt
# SLT_KAFKA_HOST_PORT=9092
# SLT_KAFKA_DOCKER_HOST_PORT=19092
# SLT_SCHEMA_REGISTRY_HOST_PORT=8081
# SLT_ZOOKEEPER_CLIENT_PORT=2181
# SLT_KAFKA_CPUS=3
# SLT_KAFKA_MEM_LIMIT=1536m
# SLT_SCHEMA_REGISTRY_CPUS=1
# SLT_SCHEMA_REGISTRY_MEM_LIMIT=1g
# SLT_ZOOKEEPER_CPUS=1
# SLT_ZOOKEEPER_MEM_LIMIT=512m
# SLT_KAFKA_VIEW_HOST=

